---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Aflora, a personal collection of interactive articles built while learning."
  translations={{ en: "/about", "pt-BR": "/pt-br/about" }}
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Aflora</p>
    <h1>A place to learn in public.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Aflora is my personal collection of interactive articles. I use it to turn
      what I am learning into something I can inspect, manipulate, and explain.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="lesson-body">
    <h2>Why this project exists</h2>
    <p>
      Writing exposes gaps in understanding. Building an interaction goes further:
      it forces the mechanism, assumptions, and edge cases to become concrete.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first article reconstructs a classification decision tree from first
      principles. It is the only article listed because Aflora's navigation reflects
      what exists today.
    </p>
    <h2>Organized around the work</h2>
    <p>
      Aflora is not a fixed curriculum or a public roadmap. Topics appear when an
      article is ready, and the library can be regrouped as the collection changes.
    </p>
    <h2>Reuse and licensing</h2>
    <p>
      Aflora's original software is available under the MIT License.
      Unless stated otherwise, original articles, newsletter issues, and educational
      illustrations are available under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>, with
      attribution to Lucca Emmanuel.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Aflora name and logo, third-party materials, and externally sourced data
      are excluded. The <a href="/licensing/">licensing page</a> records the exact
      scope and attribution guidance.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
